    "body": "Here is what I tried : \r\n\r\nWith a basic file config set to disable time module : \r\n\r\n```\r\n[time]\r\ndisabled = true\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter running `starship print-config | sed -E 's/(format.*=.*)(via.*\\$version.*)'\\''/\\1(\\2)'\\''/' > ~/.config/starship.toml` I still have the `disabled` attribute to `true` on my configuration. I haven't tested it on a complex configuration so their is maybe some edge case, but it seems this work and affects only the format attribute.",
